      "description": "Bitsocial is an open-source peer-to-peer network for social apps, with no servers, no global bans, where users and communities are cryptographic property. BSO is its native token. The vision is a network of sovereign community economies \u2014 every community owning its network, its token and its revenue \u2014 all settling in a single sound money.\n\nBSO is a fixed-supply ERC-20 on Ethereum: 210,000,000 tokens, forever. The contract is immutable and adminless \u2014 no mint, no owner, no pause, no proxy \u2014 and the entire supply was airdropped to holders, with no team allocation or presale. Usage makes the token scarcer: a share of every fee on the network burns.\n\nBitsocial Chain is the proposed Ethereum L2 appchain where this economy lives, with state derived entirely from Ethereum L1 data. Communities run their own L3s, tokens and DAOs, yet they settle, stake and pay rent in BSO, so value across the whole economy accrues to a single token.\n\nThe flagship primitives ship in the open: the .bso namespace for on-chain names and identity, community tokens paired with BSO on AgoraSwap, and programmable revenue \u2014 on-chain ad auctions that burn a share of community revenue at settlement.",
